import ../../../ui/scene_solids.dl

to check solid number {floating-point number:actual} equals {floating-point number:expected}:
    require condition ((the absolute value of (actual - expected)) < 0.00001) reporting "A shared solid mesh component changed."

to check solid {UI scene mesh:mesh} has {integer:count} triangles enclosing {floating-point number:volume}:
    require condition ((the length of mesh's indices) = (count * 3)) reporting "A solid has the wrong triangle count."
    set total to 0.0
    set index to 0
    loop while index < the length of mesh's indices:
        set first to the item at (the item at index in mesh's indices) in mesh's vertices
        set second to the item at (the item at (index + 1) in mesh's indices) in mesh's vertices
        set third to the item at (the item at (index + 2) in mesh's indices) in mesh's vertices
        set start to the UI mesh position of first
        set middle to the UI mesh position of second
        set end to the UI mesh position of third
        set area to the cross product of (middle - start) and (end - start)
        require condition ((the length of area) > 0.00000001) reporting "A solid contains a degenerate face."
        set normal to the UI mesh normal of first
        require condition ((the dot product of area and normal) > 0.0) reporting "A solid face has inward winding."
        check solid number (the length of normal) equals 1.0
        check solid number (the length of (normal - (the UI mesh normal of second))) equals 0.0
        check solid number (the length of (normal - (the UI mesh normal of third))) equals 0.0
        set total to total + (the dot product of start and (the cross product of middle and end)) / 6.0
        set index to index + 3
    check solid number total equals volume

set left to a UI point at -0.43 and 0.0
set right to a UI point at 0.43 and 0.0
set peak to a UI point at 0.0 and 0.37
set house to a UI convex prism mesh from [left, right, peak] with depth 0.76
check solid house has 8 triangles enclosing (0.86 * 0.37 * 0.76 * 0.5)
require condition ((the length of house's vertices) = 18) reporting "An extruded gable lost its independent cap or edge normals."
set reverse to a UI convex prism mesh from [peak, right, left] with depth 0.76
check solid reverse has 8 triangles enclosing (0.86 * 0.37 * 0.76 * 0.5)
set first to a UI point at -1.0 and -1.0
set second to a UI point at 1.0 and -1.0
set third to a UI point at 1.0 and 1.0
set fourth to a UI point at -1.0 and 1.0
set square to a UI convex prism mesh from [first, second, third, fourth] with depth 2.0
check solid square has 12 triangles enclosing 8.0
require condition ((the length of square's vertices) = 24) reporting "An extruded box must preserve texture seams."

set rock to a UI icosahedron mesh
check solid rock has 20 triangles enclosing 2.53615071012041
require condition ((the length of rock's vertices) = 60) reporting "A flat icosahedron must keep independent face normals."
for each vertex in rock's vertices:
    check solid number (the length of (the UI mesh position of vertex)) equals 1.0
    require condition ((0.0 <= vertex's u <= 1.0) and (0.0 <= vertex's v <= 1.0)) reporting "A solid mesh texture coordinate escaped its face."
print line "Scene solids extrude either winding of convex polygons with independent surface normals and provide unit flat-shaded icosahedra."
